    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1080,
        -460
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        690
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Trying number forms\n\nNode 8 is the whole experiment: type a number, pick what it is made of. Node 9's seed is **fixed** on purpose — change it deliberately and you can get a hand back that you liked.\n\nJudge on node 10's report, not on node 24. It says what fraction of the crop changed; over 8% means the model repainted the paper as well as writing on it, which looks fine in the preview and arrives on the sheet as a rectangle of somebody else's paper.\n\n**The reference carries a 1 and a 0.** Any other digit is the model transferring a manner, not copying a shape — that is the interesting case and also the one that fails. If a hand will not come out, 10, 13 or 31 sit in the frame exactly the same way.\n\n### Before the first run\n\n**Node 3:** `gaussblur_radius` = **3**, not its default 8. Node 2 has already grown the mask by 3 px; past ~12 px total the halo of one typed line meets the next and a paragraph becomes one hole.\n\n**Memory.** Past node 5 every IMAGE is 7440×10240 — about 900 MB of float32 each, and the typing holds three or four at once.\n\n**Nothing is resampled.** Remacri runs at its trained 4×, and the number it lands on is what the `page` directive names."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "### Trying number forms\n\nNode 8 is the whole experiment: type a number, pick what it is made of. Node 9's seed is **fixed** on purpose — change it deliberately and you can get a hand back that you liked.\n\nJudge on node 10's report, not on node 24. It says what fraction of the crop changed; over 8% means the model repainted the paper as well as writing on it, which looks fine in the preview and arrives on the sheet as a rectangle of somebody else's paper.\n\n**The reference carries a 1 and a 0.** Any other digit is the model transferring a manner, not copying a shape — that is the interesting case and also the one that fails. If a hand will not come out, 10, 13 or 31 sit in the frame exactly the same way.\n\n### Before the first run\n\n**Node 3:** `gaussblur_radius` = **3**, not its default 8. Node 2 has already grown the mask by 3 px; past ~12 px total the halo of one typed line meets the next and a paragraph becomes one hole.\n\n**Memory.** Past node 5 every IMAGE is 7440×10240 — about 900 MB of float32 each, and the typing holds three or four at once.\n\n**Nothing is resampled.** Remacri runs at its trained 4×, and the number it lands on is what the `page` directive names."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
